`GET /v1/account/oauth/authorized-applications`

Lists the OAuth applications authorized by the authenticated user.

<Tabs>
<Tab title="TypeScript">
```typescript TypeScript
photon.account.listAuthorizedApplications(input?: ListAuthorizedApplicationsInput, options?: RequestOptions): Promise<ListAuthorizedApplicationsOutput>
```
</Tab>
<Tab title="Python">
```python Python
photon.account.list_authorized_applications(input: ListAuthorizedApplicationsInput | None = None) -> models.ListAuthorizedApplicationsResponse
```
</Tab>
<Tab title="Rust">
```rust Rust
client.list_authorized_applications(params: Option<ListAuthorizedApplicationsParams>).await -> Result<ResponseValue<types::ListAuthorizedApplicationsResponse>, Error<ListAuthorizedApplicationsError>>
```
</Tab>
</Tabs>

<RequestExample>
```typescript TypeScript
import { Photon } from "@photon-ai/api";

const photon = new Photon({
  headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${process.env.PHOTON_API_TOKEN}` },
});
const result = await photon.account.listAuthorizedApplications();
```

```python Python
import os

from photon_api import Photon

photon = Photon(headers={"Authorization": f"Bearer {os.environ['PHOTON_API_TOKEN']}"})
result = photon.account.list_authorized_applications()
```

```rust Rust
use photon_ai_api::{Credential, PhotonClientBuilder, SecretString};

let token = std::env::var("PHOTON_API_TOKEN")?;
let client = PhotonClientBuilder::new()
    .credential("accountServiceKey", Credential::Bearer(SecretString::from(token)))
    .build()?;
let result = client
    .list_authorized_applications(None)
    .await
    .map_err(|error| format!("{error:?}"))?
    .into_inner();
```

</RequestExample>

